WEBVTT

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:15.390
We've got company.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.430
They're not afraid of us. They're the same lot that we're after trick and jog.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.490
Jaunt, Mike, jaunt.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.690
No, we can always do that. Let's see what they've got to say for themselves.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.480
Oh, hi there.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.980
Hey, what are you doing?

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:57.600
Mike, jaunt!

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.980
I can't...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.520
I can't!

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:49.760
Why aren't you John?

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.890
Because they've taken Chuck's metatransporter.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.230
I'd have to leave him behind.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.490
From the look of this lot, they'd get pretty nasty.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.770
Besides, I'd like to know where they're taking us.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.150
Watch yourself, Mike.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.320
I'll join along with you and keep an eye on you.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:38.920
You okay, Mike?

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.300
Yeah, so far.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:46.500
I'm just going to jaunt about a bit and have a look around the area.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.560
Unless I'm very much mistaken, that was a klepton spaceship.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.220
Klepton? Who or what are the kleptons?

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.900
Don't know very much about them, Liz, except they're a brutal race who enjoy exploiting more backward cultures.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.760
And they're almost outlaws as far as the Galactic Federation is concerned.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.260
Fortunately, they never stay in one place too long, although somewhere along the line they manage to pick up our language.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.920
They're not interested in conquest or empire building, they just come.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.360
take what they want and go.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.060
So why doesn't the Federation do something about them?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.440
They have. They've sent us here.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.900
No, I mean something official.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.880
Because, Elizabeth, Gallia, not being telepathic,

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.980
is not part of the Galactic Federation and not subject to her laws.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.090
Kleptons always take great care to stay away from planets that are members.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.280
I hope Mike knows what he's doing.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.860
Where is the object?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.340
Time for the punishment cages.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.560
But from the sound of it, things are about to turn real nicely.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.280
With the kleptons finding the hard-transporter belt, they've blown it in here.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.760
I'm not joining with that truck.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.220
Okay, give me the belt.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:48.470
Great!

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.240
I'm no Galen, haven't you guessed?

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.200
Now hand over the belt before I use this in whatever it is on you.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.480
Blast a pistol!

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.040
Be careful!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.970
In this confined space, it could kill us!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.140
Asshole! That might not be such a bad idea.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:14.550
Now release my friend. Now turn around and face the wall, all of you.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.570
And you. Go on.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:35.630
They've gone! Come on, you fools! They can't have got trouble!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:47.850
Alert from my entrance! Issue blasters to all the guards! Burn them down! Hurry, fools! Hurry!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.130
Nasty little thing.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.020
Lucky they didn't hit you with it.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.020
That's what I was thinking.

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.770
And I am thinking you ought to be more careful where you're aiming it.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:06.760
Timus?

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.660
Hey, where did you spring from?

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.660
From the galactic trig, young man.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.100
I've only a short time to spare, but I feel I owe you an explanation.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:15.360
Oh, well, shall we go through?

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:18.100
Elizabeth.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.800
It's good to see you.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.990
This is Trig and Trog, two natives of the planet, slaves from the klepton mines.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.540
Ah, so you have met the kleptons.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.160
Isn't that what you sent us here for?

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:29.980
Sent you here for?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.500
Therefore, I was under the impression that I gave you permits to come here to carry out an archaeological survey.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.400
Oh, pull the other one. It's got bells on.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:44.000
The other one? Pull. Bells on. Please, show me which one to pull.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:44.980
Oh, forget it.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:51.000
Mike Means, we all know you engineered our visit here so we'd meet the kleptons. It was no accident.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:55.790
Yes, Elizabeth, you are right. Now, please, listen quickly.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.950
I have not much time. My absence will be noticed if I stay too long.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:01.210
Thank you.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:08.520
You know that some of us are dissatisfied with the way the Galactic Federation Council

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.280
will devote a lot of energy to talking about a problem,

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.190
but is always most reluctant to take any action.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.240
That is why the kleptons have got away for so long

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.120
with their antisocial practice of invading planets

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.960
and using the local inhabitants as slave labour

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.260
to help them strip the planet of its resources.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.190
Oh, the council is aware of the problem.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.010
There is even a subcommittee in existence which has been discussing what to do about the kleptons for more than 200 of your Earth years.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:41.610
Yes, and meanwhile, the kleptons continue to murder, enslave and steal.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.500
How long have the kleptons been on Gallia?

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.750
Elizabeth, would you repeat your question?

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.600
How long have the kleptons been on Gallia?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:07.310
It was two summers ago when the star fell from the sky and the evil men stepped from it.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.170
That is about three and a half years in your timescale.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.000
But he can speak English.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:15.320
We spent all this time trying to teach him and to learn Gallia in ourselves.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.370
Yes, it's a little gift I have.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.480
So men of the village went to greet them.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:21.960
My father was one.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.040
They never returned.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.180
The kleptons cured them.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.720
Thus a nostrachrin they came to the village and took all the boys to work in their mine.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.160
Why take the boys?

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:29.980
That's what I can't understand.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.950
I mean, surely they'd get more work done with adult slaves.

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.930
Well, I can think of a reason straight away.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:38.080
Some of those seams and passages in the rock are so narrow

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.860
that only the children could work in them.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.180
But that is not the main reason.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.390
I am afraid that affection for one's children is universal,

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.800
and the kleptons exploit this wherever they go.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.360
The galleons are not a cowardly people.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.500
They might rise up against the kleptons,

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.880
even though they have only primitive weapons.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.480
The men would not be afraid to die.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:09:59.980
But one thing...

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.520
Almost every Galleon family has at least one child imprisoned in that mine.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:11.150
As well as being slaves, they are also hostages.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.530
But why were the villagers afraid when they saw us?

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.670
You think they'd be glad to see us if they thought we'd escape from the mine?

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.280
No, I did not know you were going to the village.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.040
If we escape and the kleptons catch us, then they punish not just us,

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:27.860
but also the child of anyone who helps us, who gives us food and shelter.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:29.980
The people of our village are not afraid.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.280
of you but of what the kleptons do to their children if they helped you nasty

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:40.430
what are the kleptons digging from that mine anyway this crystalline carbon in

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.960
the form you would call a diamond well he doesn't look much like a diamond to me

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:48.930
it's a diamond all right Mike it's not being cut yet that's all do you know

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.550
back on earth this would be worth hundreds of thousands of pounds it'll

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.240
make a big splash then won't it why don't throw it away Mike well what goods

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:58.250
a diamond to us a stupid hole up a crystalline carbon you can't eat it

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.930
Oh, you've changed your tune. You wanted a treasure.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.840
when you first came here? Since then, I've been down in the mine and seen how these things are dug out.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.720
I sympathize with Mike. Diamonds are supposed to be a girl's best friend,

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.260
but not if they're dragged out by children in chains.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:15.250
No. Good riddance for bad rubbish. Now, what are we going to do about those

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:21.750
kleptons? Timers, what would you like us to do?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.040
Of course, in my position, I can't really say.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.420
As far as I am concerned, you are here on an archaeological expedition.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.670
The Federation Council, of which I am a representative,

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.600
would not countenance any action to interfere with events on a primitive planet.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:49.500
Timus, don't go all official and stuffy on us. What do you want us to do?

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.020
I think that's obvious, don't you?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:57.070
Set the slaves free, send the kleptons packing and make sure they don't return.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.970
And let the people of this planet get on with living their life.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.080
lives in peace now I must go my absence from the council will be noticed if

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:12.300
you'll excuse me I know that you will manage far better without my help my

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:23.760
blessings on your enterprise well we're on our own John them kids in my

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:27.700
muscle as I do about the kleptons maybe they'd like the opportunity to get their

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:28.040
own back

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:07.040
Now, the plan is to get all the slaves out of the mine

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.060
before the kleptons wake up and realise what's going on.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.600
I'd like to use these things on those kleptons.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.610
It's more permanent than the stun gun.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.850
Even if you took it, Mike, you couldn't use it.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:16.930
You can't kill, remember?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:19.300
Not even creatures as evil as the kleptons.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:20.360
More's the pity.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:21.620
Now, listen, it's important.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:22.900
We all know exactly what we're doing.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.830
Now, we know from what Trigger's told us

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.810
that the kleptons sleep in the spaceship.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:29.980
Now, that's a fair...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.200
from the mine entrance. There will be one or two kleptons on guard inside the mine

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:37.960
but they'll be expecting an escape from the inside not an attack from the outside.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.770
Nevertheless those kleptons will have to be dealt with and by that I mean stunned Mike.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:49.180
It'll be a pleasure. Once inside the mine we get all the slaves free. When and only when

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:53.360
all the slaves are safely outside we deal with the rest of the kleptons, us three.

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:59.770
Understand? Now Trig and Trog know the mine best so once inside we'll follow their directions.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.150
What are we doing?

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:04.630
Nothing to stop us, except we've only got one transporter belt.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.110
And the best way to make sure all the kleptons are put safely to sleep

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.410
is to approach on foot from the outside.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:37.440
God, you'll be double, because there is good reason to believe there are alien intruders on this planet.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:41.070
They must be here to steal our diamonds.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:45.290
Whoever they are, they are not just primitive peasants.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.680
They are sophisticated with the technology to match our own.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.790
So, to your both.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.820
Now, they outnumber us, and they outgun us.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:14:59.900
The one advantage we have is surprise.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.260
Let's keep it that way, okay? Everybody ready?

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:11.710
Head on to this place if we don't come back.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.190
Force Field will remain in operation for thousands of years,

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.550
until the galleons develop a technology advanced enough to penetrate it.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.580
By then, it'll probably have become a place of great and ancient mystery.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.860
They'll probably think it contains all the secrets of the universe,

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.920
instead of just some out-of-date fossilized campaign.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:33.600
Don't be so morbid. We're bound to come back.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:36.250
Let's hope so.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:43.760
There's two guards out there.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.680
You take the one on the right, I'll take the one on the left.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:47.510
Okay.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:48.610
Ready?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:49.740
Yep.

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:35.680
Hi!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.770
Emergency alert. Emergency alert.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.310
That's the last one.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:10.140
Good. All we've got to do now is get them out of here.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.160
Still gone very smoothly so far.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.560
Yeah, too smoothly for my liking.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:16.890
Mike, Liz and I are going to the mine entrance. You and Trigg, bring them along.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:31.440
What is it?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.480
Kleptons. And one of them's got a blaster pistol.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.300
Get these kids under cover, Liz. Get those kids under cover.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:40.140
Kleptons?

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:41.220
Yeah, about three of them.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:44.260
Liz, get the kids deeper into the mine. Find a safe place to hide.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.350
Fight for a reload!

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.920
No, I want Gremlond.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.490
Pistol, or I will kill the child's slaves.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.330
Over there, the others.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:15.930
Hurry! Mike will pay for what you have done.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.430
Mike! Mike!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:40.120
Is it true there are only three of you?

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:44.350
Yes, but don't go getting any ideas. You've seen what we can do.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:49.250
I shall never understand the ways of the Galactic Federation people.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:58.610
Firstly, if we had won, you would not be alive now, and yet you are letting us go.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.320
Secondly, being able to win so easily, why did you wait so long in coming?

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:14.380
Just take it that we're different, and we're not exactly letting you go.

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:19.750
Your ship is to be transferred by instant matter transporter to a planet called Styxus.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:23.530
Your engines have been removed and your communications equipment destroyed.

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:28.880
As far as I'm concerned, you and your men are going to spend the rest of eternity on Styxus.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.980
a pretty bleak eternity it's going to be

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.660
from now on. One day

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:36.020
we will escape from this planet

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:38.620
Styxus, and when we do

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:41.160
the vengeance of Klepton will

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.190
sweep you away. That's as

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.960
maybe. Time you were going, Captain. Your flight is

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.320
called. I will be back

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.800
tomorrow, person.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.240
Styxus is a pretty nasty

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:59.590
planet. The Kleptons won't have an easy time

00:21:59.590 --> 00:21:59.830
there.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:07.180
very little but rock and rain they will have to forage for their food and they won't find much

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:12.950
only moss and lichens clinging to the rocks and they'll get a pretty nasty shock when they open

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:17.460
up their holes to look at their food supplies unfortunately they had to leave most of their

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:23.210
stocks behind in order to make room for their more essential supplies what more essential supplies

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:29.780
diamonds took a long time to dig them out for them we wouldn't want you to cut

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.280
to leave them behind. Diamonds won't be much

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:34.180
used to them on Stixas. Not unless they can

00:22:34.180 --> 00:22:35.300
find some way to cook them.

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:38.940
How have you got strong teeth? Oh, and by the way,

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:41.060
Thomas, I have here our report for the

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:43.240
Galactic Federation about our interesting

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:44.800
but uneventful archaeological

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.420
survey on Gallia. I've got to hand it to you, Thomas.

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:49.660
This was a really great place to come for a holiday.

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:51.510
But how about butlin sticks, do you reckon?

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:54.120
Butlins? Is that in the Galactic Federation?

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:01.370
Thank you.
